--- WHAT SHIPPED (parity port of the web LinearSidebar) ---
4-file shared-surface pattern, all bound to the shared P1/S8 seams + P1/S10 i18n facade; the view performs
no router/storage I/O and reads every label from the projection:
  * LinearSidebar.Model.cs      — Registration (Slug + 8 i18n keys/fallbacks + 3 trailing-badge route literals
                                   + {{count}}/{{page}}/{0} interpolators + 99+ chip cap), data records
                                   (LinearNavItem/Section), projected display records, the pure
                                   LinearSidebarProjection (active-path test, whitespace tokenizer, every-token
                                   match, favorites-resolve, trailing-badge routing, collapse + filter-expand),
                                   and the PII-safe LinearSidebarDiagnostics (emits only view.opened slug).
  * LinearSidebar.Source.cs     — P1/S8 seams: INavLocationSource (web useLocation) + IPinnedPagesStore
                                   (web pinnedItems source + onPin/onUnpin), each with an in-memory impl.
  * LinearSidebar.ViewModel.cs  — INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable holder: collapse set seeded to
                                   "everything except the active section" + auto-expand on active change,
                                   tree filter, pin/unpin via the store, controlled pathname over live location.
  * LinearSidebar.cs            — WinUI 3 ContentControl: navigation landmark, always-visible Favorites group,
                                   collapsible sections as Expanders, 2px active accent + medium weight,
                                   trailing unread-dot / count-chip, hover/focus-revealed pin/unpin actions,
                                   and the empty-filter "No matches." + "Clear filter" branch announced via a
                                   polite live region. Tokenized brushes (DisplayTokens, P1/S9) — no inline hex.

STATES REPRODUCED: Tree (favorites + collapsible sections + active accent + trailing badges) and EmptyFilter
("No matches." + Clear filter). The web source is presentational — its tree/favorites arrive as props and its
only hooks are useLocation + useTranslation, so it performs NO data fetch and therefore has NO loading / error /
stale / offline chrome to reproduce (documented in the surface XML docs, mirroring siblings EndpointSidebar /
SearchInput). Accessibility: Navigation landmark + Narrator name on every interactive element; decorative
glyphs/dots marked AccessibilityView.Raw; system font scale honoured via text primitives; nothing animated
beyond the Expander reveal (reduced-motion safe). Telemetry: view.opened slug=LinearSidebar (P1/S11).

i18n (P1/S10): every surface-owned string flows through ILocalizer. Added the 7 missing nav.* keys to
Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw in sorted position (nav.unpinPage already present): nav.sidebar,
nav.favorites, nav.filterNoMatch, nav.filterClear, nav.vehicleCount, nav.staleCount, nav.pinPage. Values follow
the existing per-locale convention (the catalog currently carries English placeholders for every nav.* key in
ar/he, e.g. nav.vehicles=Fleet, nav.unpinPage="Unpin {0}").

